# Kapare SDLC (ChalkIQ)

**Canonical playbook:** [/Users/mbp/brain/projects/deep-onboarding.md](/Users/mbp/brain/projects/deep-onboarding.md)

Read it when starting work, planning features, or before claiming a task is done. ChalkIQ-specific commands and paths: `docs/DEVELOPMENT.md` · ticket template: `docs/agentic/tickets/CHALK-000-example.md`

## Workflow

Use **6-step lite** (T0–T1, simple T2) or **full 13-step Kapare** (T2 with risk, all T3–T4) per deep-onboarding. Always declare **tier (T0–T4)** before implementing.

```text
 1 Slicer → 2 StoryWeaver → 3 Challenger → 4 Planner → 5 Test Architect (T3+)
 7 Builder → 8 Test Green → 9 Verifier → 10 Bugbot (T3+) → 11 Dockeeper → 12 Integrator → 13 Shipper
```

**Loopback:** If step 8, 9, or 10 fails → return to step 7 (Builder). If Challenger rejects stories → return to step 2.

## ChalkIQ context

- **App:** Sports prediction — Python, Vercel landing + API, autonomous GitHub Actions pipeline
- **Live:** https://chalkiq.com · https://chalk-iq.streamlit.app/ (Streamlit secondary)
- **Scope:** Men's CBB + CFB only — see `docs/CFB_STRATEGY.md`, `docs/AUTOMATION.md`
- **Tickets:** `docs/agentic/tickets/CHALK-NNN-short-name.md`
- **Plans:** `docs/agentic/work/CHALK-NNN/plan.md` (T2+ risk, all T3+)

## Tier quick reference

| Tier | Examples in ChalkIQ | Tests | Pipeline |
|------|---------------------|-------|----------|
| T0 | README, comments | None | 6-step lite |
| T1 | Landing page styling | None | 6-step lite + pre-ship |
| T2 | Admin UI, subscribe form | Smoke optional | 6-step lite + pre-ship |
| T3 | Elo, slate, CLV, backtest, player ratings | **TDD required** | Full 13-step + Bugbot |
| T4 | Stripe, Postgres, auth, PII | TDD + security-review | Full 13-step |

## Verify before "done"

```bash
bash scripts/pre-ship.sh
```

T3+: confirm new/updated tests exist under `tests/` and pass.

## Human gates (never skip)

Do **not** commit, push, open PR, merge, or deploy unless the user explicitly asks.

## Agent behavior

- Propose tier and current Kapare step at the start of non-trivial tasks
- On T3+ diffs, run Bugbot before claiming ship-ready
- On T4 diffs, run security-review before claiming ship-ready
